<item>
            <title>[LU-20592] nfs server doesn&apos;t load dir layout when accessing Lustre striped dirs by filehandle.</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20592</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Sometimes reading of  a Lustre striped dir through  an NFS-share goes wrong way using&lt;br/&gt;
mdc_read_page() directly instead of using lmv_striped_page_read() and splitting the readdir between the striped on the client side.  &lt;br/&gt;
On the server, the read page is handed using lod_striped_it_ops and it hits a bug fixed by &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19798&quot; title=&quot;osp_md_index_it_next() may reference wrong page &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19798&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19798&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, see &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15487&quot; title=&quot;crash after mdd_dir_page_build() error&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15487&quot;&gt;LU-15487&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looks like the striping info is not available at the moment of doing lmv_read_page() and Lustre client deals with a striped dir as with a plain one.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
